TITLE: DG-1A-AR-H135 — Debt-Family Reactivation / Shared Re-Audition Economy Preregistration
DATE: 2026-09-19
STATUS: PREREGISTERED / SYNTHETIC / UNEXECUTED
TRACK: DG-1A / ADAPTIVE-RULE RESEARCH
BRANCH: dg1a-ar
PARENT: dg1a-arh134-representation-debt-compaction-audit.ice

PURPOSE

H134 showed that representation-debt markers can be compressed into fit-gated debt families while retaining high future recall and reducing storage.

H135 asks:

WHEN ONE DORMANT DEBT-FAMILY MEMBER BECOMES HIGH VALUE,

can shared family structure reduce the evidence cost of re-auditing related unresolved sites

WITHOUT

turning one local cue into broad false promotion?

BOUNDARY

This is synthetic research only.

It does not:
- implement biological tissue;
- establish a production architecture;
- freeze a representation metric;
- execute or modify STAB-18-R1;
- spend canonical scientific execution;
- authorize deployment or runtime activation.

EVIDENCE CLASS TARGET

SYNTHETIC
MEASURED_SANDBOX

PRIMARY HYPOTHESIS

A fit-gated canary reactivation policy will dominate both:
- isolated individual re-audition on evidence efficiency; and
- unconditional family broadcast on false-promotion control.

The expected mechanism is:

1. reactivate a small canary subset from the debt family;
2. measure fresh residual agreement under the current context;
3. broadcast re-audition only if canary agreement clears a preregistered fit gate;
4. otherwise fall back to local/member-specific re-audition.

SYNTHETIC ECOLOGY

Each world contains:
- 8 to 14 latent debt families;
- 18 to 70 dormant members per family;
- a stored family prototype in a low-dimensional residual space;
- member-specific local offsets;
- heterogeneous current member value;
- fresh context drift after dormancy.

Reactivation events are sampled from four preregistered regimes:

R1 — FAMILY-STABLE
The whole family remains approximately valid under current context.

R2 — SINGLE-MEMBER-DRIFT
One or a few members have drifted away while the family remains otherwise coherent.

R3 — SUBGROUP-DRIFT
A coherent minority subgroup has changed.

R4 — WHOLE-FAMILY-SHIFT
Most members have shifted together to a new residual regime.

Rare families receive extra sampling weight so current frequency cannot substitute for future value.

COMPARATORS

A — INDIVIDUAL
Re-audit only the triggering member.
No family sharing.

B — BLIND BROADCAST
One trigger causes wide family re-audition without a fresh fit check.

C — FIXED CANARY
Audit a fixed small canary subset, then broadcast when canary agreement is high.

D — FIT-GATED ADAPTIVE CANARY
Choose a small diverse canary subset.
Estimate current family fit from canary agreement and dispersion.
Broadcast only when the gate passes.
Otherwise remain local or split the challenged subgroup.

E — FULL FAMILY CHECK
Audit all family members before deciding.
Upper-bound evidence quality with high evidence cost.

PRIMARY WORKING PARAMETERS

Primary confirmation worlds: 2,000.

Canary fraction:
max(3 members, approximately 10% of family), capped at 7.

Broadcast fit gate:
fresh canary agreement >= 0.80
AND
normalized canary dispersion <= 0.65.

Local promotion gate:
member fresh-fit score >= 0.75.

Incorrect promotion cost:
5.0 value units per falsely promoted member.

Correctly resolved member benefit:
3.0 value units.

Evidence cost:
1.0 per audited member.

Broadcast application cost:
0.20 per member reached after a passing gate.

Dormant unresolved carry cost:
0.15 per still-unresolved high-value member.

The numerical scale is synthetic and only supports policy comparison inside this toy ecology.

PRIMARY METRICS

1. net future value;
2. evidence audits consumed;
3. correctly resolved high-value members;
4. false promotions;
5. false-promotion rate among promoted members;
6. family-level coverage;
7. local-drift containment;
8. whole-family-shift recovery;
9. cost per correctly resolved member.

PRIMARY ACCEPTANCE SHAPE

The fit-gated adaptive-canary policy is considered supported only if, in primary confirmation:

- mean net value exceeds INDIVIDUAL;
- mean net value exceeds BLIND BROADCAST;
- mean evidence consumption is less than FULL FAMILY CHECK;
- false-promotion rate is less than BLIND BROADCAST;
- FAMILY-STABLE coverage exceeds 85%;
- SINGLE-MEMBER-DRIFT false promotion remains below 10%;
- WHOLE-FAMILY-SHIFT recovery exceeds INDIVIDUAL coverage;
- result is not dependent on one narrow canary fraction or one exact threshold.

FAILURE CONDITIONS

Treat H135 as negative or mixed if:
- canaries frequently miss subgroup drift;
- broadcast savings disappear after false-promotion penalties;
- the fit gate simply approximates a full-family scan;
- performance collapses under modest threshold perturbation;
- whole-family shifts cannot be detected without nearly full evidence expenditure.

ROBUSTNESS SWEEPS

Canary fractions:
approximately 5%, 10%, 20%.

Agreement gates:
0.70, 0.80, 0.90.

Dispersion gates:
0.50, 0.65, 0.80.

Drift prevalence:
low, medium, high.

Family size:
small, medium, large.

Additional stress:
- canaries accidentally drawn from one local subgroup;
- stale stored family prototype;
- one high-value member contradicts the majority;
- entire family context changes coherently.

INTERPRETATION GUARDRAIL

A positive result would support:

SHARED DEBT MEMORY
+
SMALL FRESH EVIDENCE PROBE
+
CONDITIONAL BROADCAST

not unconditional family promotion.

A negative result would imply that H134 compression remains useful for storage, but family membership is not sufficient to share re-audition evidence.

FROZEN BEFORE EXECUTION

The comparators, primary metrics, main parameter scale, acceptance shape, and robustness dimensions above are fixed before synthetic execution.

Do not execute STAB-18-R1 during this lane.

